                     Autoscaling

--> Autoscaling is an AWS feature that monitor and automatically increse and decrese number of server based on demand.

--> Types of Autoscaling 
1. Horizontal Scaling
2. Vertical scaling

1. Horizontal scaling: (autoscaling) : Automatic
--> Adding or removing instances.
--> scale out : add more server
--> scale in : remove instances

2. Vertical scaling : manual
--> increasing or decresing the capacity of the same instance. 
--> scale up : upgread to a larger type.
--> scale in : downgread to a smaller instance type.

Stress command:
--> the stres command is used to generate artifical load on a linux system by stressing CPU, memory and disk.
--> it is maninly bused for testing
--> install stress command
yum install stress -y

syntax:
stress --cpu 2 -t 60
here,
stress : command to generate load
--cpu : create CPU stress workers
2 : create 2 workers that continuously perform calculation
-t : timeline
60 : give load for 60 seconds


